<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-planform-morphology-animation> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "PlanformDB planarian morphology animation faithfully reproduces Planaria (Schmidtea mediterranea, Dugesia japonica) morphology" ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) 2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Planaria (Schmidtea mediterranea, Dugesia japonica) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 66.5/100, audit 2026-10-14-morphology-audit) and the assessments." ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/161f269/2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py; output: planform_morphology_gallery.png; organism: Planaria (Schmidtea mediterranea, Dugesia japonica); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/161f269; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.bpj.2017.04.011>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1093/bioinformatics/btt088>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/bio.20123400> ;
    pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-14-morphology-audit-planform-morphology-animation-code-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-14-morphology-audit-planform-morphology-animation-model-fidelity>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-14-morphology-audit-planform-morphology-animation-morphometric-validation>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-14-morphology-audit-planform-morphology-animation-overall>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-14-morphology-audit-planform-morphology-animation-parameter-expressivity>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-14-morphology-audit-planform-morphology-animation-repro-package>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-14-morphology-audit-planform-morphology-animation-source-traceability>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-14-morphology-audit-planform-morphology-animation-specimen-match> ;
    pk:weightOfEvidence 6.65e-01 .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-14-morphology-audit-planform-morphology-animation-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "PlanformDB planarian morphology animation — Code-to-model traceability: 75/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "The decoding rule, the coordinate convention (+y anterior, wild-type head->trunk angle 3pi/2) and the cartoon convention are documented where they are implemented, and region_outline() names the figure it reproduces. The radii-count rule was established by checking the database rather than quoted from a numbered equation, because the papers describe the formalism in prose. Evidence: 2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py L35–L38: coordinate convention <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/161f269/2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py#L35-L38>; 2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py L321–L331: region_outline() docstring: arc construction and Fig. 1D <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/161f269/2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py#L321-L331>; 2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py L211–L244: load_first_report_year(): experiment->publication join documented <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/161f269/2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py#L211-L244>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-planform-morphology-animation-code-traceability> ;
    pk:hasProbability 7.5e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-14-morphology-audit-planform-morphology-animation-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "PlanformDB planarian morphology animation — Model fidelity to source: 85/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Region shape parameters are interpreted with the formalism's own rule (0 links -> 4 radii right/anterior/left/posterior; 1 link -> +90/+180/+270 deg from the edge; k >= 2 links -> one radius per bisector of consecutive edges), region centres are placed from the RegionsLink Dist/Ang labels and borders at Ratio*Dist, and the rule is checked at load time against all 1181 regions in the database. The only element not taken from the source is how consecutive control radii are joined: a superellipse arc (n = 2.2 free, n = 7 at a border) chosen to reproduce Planform's Fig. 1D; the paper does not publish Planform's interpolant. Evidence: 2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py L20–L34: formalism as implemented, with the radii-count rule <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/161f269/2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py#L20-L34>; 2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py L286–L314: control_points(): radii -> directions per link count <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/161f269/2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py#L286-L314>; 2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py L248–L272: layout(): centres from Dist/Ang, borders from Ratio <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/161f269/2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py#L248-L272>; 2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py L701–L715: check_encoding(): 1181/1181 regions obey the rule <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/161f269/2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py#L701-L715>; 2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py L317–L355: superellipse interpolant between radii (not from the source) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/161f269/2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py#L317-L355>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-planform-morphology-animation-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:hasProbability 8.5e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-14-morphology-audit-planform-morphology-animation-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "PlanformDB planarian morphology animation — Morphometric validation: 45/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "The script computes silhouette morphometrics (AP length, ML width, aspect, area, region and organ counts, length relative to wild type) for every morphology and can write them as CSV, and the measurements sidecar checks the decoded wild type against the radii encoded in the database (560 x 120 units). Nothing is yet compared with measurements of real animals or with values reported in the literature; the reference is the formalism, not a specimen. Evidence: 2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py L386–L412: morphometrics() <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/161f269/2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py#L386-L412>; 2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py L684–L698: write_csv() <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/161f269/2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py#L684-L698>; 2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py L713–L714: wild-type AP/ML printed at load <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/161f269/2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py#L713-L714>. Measurements (measure_outputs.py): wild-type silhouette AP length = 557.6 Planform units (reference 560, PlanformDB 2.5.0 RegionParam/RegionsLink of morphology 1 (80+200+200+80)) [union of decoded region outlines of Morphology 1, rasterised; bbox extent along the AP axis]; wild-type silhouette ML width = 119.8 Planform units (reference 120, trunk lateral radii 60+60) [as above, across the ML axis]; wild-type AP/ML aspect = 4.653 ratio (reference 4.667, encoded radii) [AP length / ML width of the decoded silhouette] — S. mediterranea in Lobo et al. 2013 Fig. 1A is of this order; the formalism, not a specimen, is the reference; morphologies rendered = 369 count [Morphology rows with at least one encoded region] — 372 rows in the database; 3 have no regions (Lethal, Midbody Buldge, Double head, side tail); distinct body silhouettes = 167 count (reference 369, upper bound: one silhouette per morphology) [unique (AP length, ML width, area to 100 units, #heads, #tails) tuples over all rendered morphologies] — 115 morphologies share the wild-type body and differ only in organs (ectopic eyes, doubled CNS, pharynx position, ...), which is how the database encodes them; distinct encodings (regions + links + organs) = 369 count (reference 369, every morphology row is a distinct phenotype) [unique tuples of every encoded number read from the database]; IoU wild type vs double head (#24) = 0.8884 ratio (reference < 1; the two bodies differ only at the posterior cap (tail -> second head), the rest of the difference is organs) [intersection-over-union of the two decoded silhouettes on a shared canvas (region centres aligned by layout)]; IoU wild type vs headless (#20) = 0.6116 ratio (reference ≈ (trunk+tail area)/(whole-body area) if the head is simply absent) [as above]." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-planform-morphology-animation-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:hasProbability 4.5e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-14-morphology-audit-planform-morphology-animation-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "PlanformDB planarian morphology animation — MorphoEval overall 66.5/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Rewritten. The region graph of every PlanformDB morphology is now decoded exactly (polar radii per region, centres and borders from the RegionsLink labels, organs from the organ table) and drawn in Planform's own cartoon convention; wild type, double head, headless, cyclops and the other canonical phenotypes are visually distinct and recognisable as Planform drawings. Remaining gap: the formalism stores three radii per head, so species features such as auricles or a triangular head are not in the data and the renders still read as cartoons, not specimens. Overall 66.5/100 (faithfulness 66.1, reproducibility 67.3); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 161f269; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 85, Morphological realism / specimen match 60, Parameter expressivity 75, Morphometric validation 45, Source and data traceability 70, Code-to-model traceability 75, Reproducibility package 60. Output judged: planform_morphology_gallery.png: rendered output of 2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py at 161f269, image/png, 443915 B, 1920×2160 px, sha256 77a7dfa087bf89441dc35c64bc0c96bccfdc15d44a3d600df766fb723a87ace5." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-planform-morphology-animation> ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Add per-species outline templates (auricles, head shape) layered on the decoded regions, clearly marked as not from the database.",
        "remediation needed: Compare the decoded aspect ratio and organ positions with measurements on photographed S. mediterranea / D. japonica.",
        "remediation needed: Pin dependency versions for the Python 3.14 environment used here.",
        "remediation needed: Record the sha256 and version of the PlanformDB file used, and its download location." ;
    pk:hasProbability 6.65e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-14-morphology-audit-planform-morphology-animation-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "PlanformDB planarian morphology animation — Parameter expressivity: 75/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Every encoded quantity now has a visible effect: each radius moves one control point of its region, each link moves a region centre and a border, each organ vector/rotation places one organ. All morphologies in a frame share one scale (frame_bounds), so the size and proportion differences between phenotypes are preserved. The final morphospace grid of the timeline fits each morphology to its cell, which deliberately trades scale for legibility. Evidence: 2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py L525–L531: frame_bounds(): common scale within a frame <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/161f269/2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py#L525-L531>; 2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py L546–L565: render_gallery(): small multiples at common scale <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/161f269/2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py#L546-L565>; 2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py L572–L681: render_timeline(): per-year pages, final grid fitted per cell <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/161f269/2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py#L572-L681>; planform_morphospace_timeline.gif (generated output, not in repo): 68 frames: intro, 30 year pages, final morphospace grid of 359 dated morphologies — planform_morphospace_timeline.gif: rendered output of 2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py at 161f269, image/gif, 3265519 B, 1500×780 px, 63 frames, sha256 f7c8cadf3c06c8351a49b6a47e1fc73fafafa7b430841771c14806fe54ce92a4." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-planform-morphology-animation-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:hasProbability 7.5e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-14-morphology-audit-planform-morphology-animation-repro-package> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "PlanformDB planarian morphology animation — Reproducibility package: 60/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Deterministic (no random state), invocation documented in the docstring and README, outputs reproduced identically on re-run, and morphologies with no encoded regions are skipped with a message rather than failing. Dependencies (numpy, scipy, matplotlib, Pillow) are in requirements.txt with lower bounds only, and the run depends on an unversioned external database. Evidence: 2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py L40–L43: documented invocation <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/161f269/2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py#L40-L43>; 2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py L196–L202: region-less morphologies skipped explicitly <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/161f269/2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py#L196-L202>; requirements.txt L1–L7: lower-bound pins only <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/161f269/requirements.txt#L1-L7>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-planform-morphology-animation-repro-package> ;
    pk:hasProbability 6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-14-morphology-audit-planform-morphology-animation-source-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "PlanformDB planarian morphology animation — Source and data traceability: 70/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Both source papers are cited with DOIs in the module docstring, the database version is named and the schema tables used are listed. The database itself is still an external file located through PLANFORM_DB_PATH; no hash or download URL is recorded, so the exact input cannot be verified from the repository alone. Evidence: 2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py L10–L16: DOIs of both Lobo et al. 2013 papers <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/161f269/2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py#L10-L16>; 2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py L138–L146: resolve_db_path(): env var or CLI, no provenance recorded <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/161f269/2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py#L138-L146>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-planform-morphology-animation-source-traceability> ;
    pk:hasProbability 7e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-14-morphology-audit-planform-morphology-animation-specimen-match> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "PlanformDB planarian morphology animation — Morphological realism / specimen match: 60/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "Side by side with Planform's Fig. 1D (Biology Open) the wild type now has the same structure: a straight-sided body with flat head/trunk and trunk/tail borders, rounded caps, red head fading to pink, blue tail, oval eyes with pupils, green brain lobes and nerve cords, a tube pharynx. Double head (#24), headless (#20), cyclops, side heads and polarity-reversed morphologies are told apart at a glance; 167 distinct body silhouettes among 369 morphologies, the rest (115 of them wild-type bodied) differing only in organs, which is how the database encodes them. Against a photographed S. mediterranea the match is weaker: no auricles, no triangular head, no pigmentation; these are not encoded in the database. Evidence: planform_morphology_gallery.png (generated output, not in repo): 16 canonical phenotypes compared with Planform Fig. 1D and the Planform screenshots in Lobo et al. 2013 — planform_morphology_gallery.png: rendered output of 2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py at 161f269, image/png, 443915 B, 1920×2160 px, sha256 77a7dfa087bf89441dc35c64bc0c96bccfdc15d44a3d600df766fb723a87ace5; 2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py L78–L87: Planform colour convention <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/161f269/2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py#L78-L87>; 2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py L460–L510: draw_morphology(): outline, gradient fills, organs <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/161f269/2013-lobo-planform-morphology.py#L460-L510>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-planform-morphology-animation-specimen-match> ;
    pk:hasProbability 6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

